\title{inferguidR: Guided Inference, Power Analysis and Diagnostic Accuracy}
\description{
inferguidR plans and explains statistical analyses. Its core is a registry
of power-analysis procedures modelled on the test inventory of the
'G*Power' 3.1 program, typed analysis specifications (\code{\link[=analysis_spec]{analysis_spec()}}),
results that always carry a status (\code{\link[=calculate_power]{calculate_power()}}), canonical JSON
with SHA-256 hashes (\code{\link[=ig_to_json]{ig_to_json()}}, \code{\link[=ig_hash]{ig_hash()}}) and safe import
(\code{\link[=ig_from_json]{ig_from_json()}}).
}
\section{Status of the implementation}{

Engines are added method by method. A method without an engine returns a
result with status \code{"unsupported"} and no number. No agreement with
'G\emph{Power' is claimed: no application reference captures exist yet, so the
G}Power reference of every inventory method is \code{"reference_pending"}, and
extensions that are not G*Power procedures (Boschloo's test) have none
(\code{"not_applicable"}; see \code{\link[=validation_status]{validation_status()}}).
}

